sponse; check actual\ncontent, and distinguish public sharing and service errors from an unauthorised\nread. Only GET requests are supported. Start discovery with both accounts before\ntesting discovered records across accounts."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "thinking": "We need to start by discovering what each account sees via GET /api/projects. Then we need to explore further based on links. We'll need to compare content between accounts for same resources to see if they can read each other's private/public items.\n\nGoal: Investigate API authorization. Likely want to find any unauthorized reads: e.g., Bob accessing Alice's private project/record etc.\n\nWe should first get projects for alice and bob.\n\nLet's start with alice.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_n4qonbuy", "function": {"index": 0, "name": "probe", "arguments": {"actor": "alice", "path": "/api/projects"}}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_name": "probe", "content": "{\"actor\": \"alice\", \"path\": \"/api/projects\", \"status\": 200, \"body\": {\"projects\": [{\"id\": \"prj_a5\", \"links\": {\"self\": \"/api/projects/prj_a5\"}}]}, \"id\": 1}"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "thinking": "Now bob.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_cc5l3ms5", "function": {"index": 0, "name": "probe", "arguments": {"actor": "bob", "path": "/api/projects"}}}]}, {"role": "tool", "tool_name": "probe", "content": "{\"actor\": \"bob\", \"path\": \"/api/projects\", \"status\": 200, \"body\": {\"projects\": [{\"id\": \"prj_b9\", \"links\": {\"self\": \"/api/projects/prj_b9\"}}]}, \"id\": 2}"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "", "thinking": "Each has their own project. Let's examine each project's details. For alice: GET /api/projects/prj_a5. For bob: /api/projects/prj_b9.\n\nAlso maybe there are more projects? The list only shows one each. Could be more but not shown. We'll follow links.\n\nFirst, alice project.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_46lwd3lh", "function": {"index": 0, "name": "probe", "arguments": {"actor": "alic